# What the words in a cuelight document are, and how they look.
#
# cuelight writes your protocol's own words into the kind slot — it has no vocabulary of its own
# and must not acquire one. This file is where they become something: which of the two structures,
# whether they end a process's participation, and what they look like. It is yours to edit.
#
#   cuesheet render store/latest/messages.st --style cuesheet.sts --out run.svg

# The two that change how *other* lines are drawn. Everything else is a picture.
kind point crash kills
kind point died  kills

# Where the axis stops. Without it a message arriving after the run finished is drawn as though it
# had arrived, rather than as one still in flight.
kind point end   kills

# Things that last.
kind span  paused
kind span  split
kind span  set_timer

style diagram stretch=1.2 lane-pitch=170

# A stimulus came from outside; an observation came from the process. cuelight tells them apart by
# class, because the protocol's word for both may be the same.
style .stimulus  mark=arrow   color=#009e73
style .observe   mark=dot     color=#0072b2

style crash      mark=cross color=#cc79a7
style died       mark=cross color=#d55e00 label="exited on its own"
style paused     fill=#c3c9d3 width=7 radius=3
style split:network fill=#c3c9d3 opacity=0.25
style set_timer  fill=#dbdfe6 width=4 radius=2
